{"date_raw": "16/09/2025", "meeting_date": "2025-09-16", "location": "Brussels", "organizations_raw": "Women Political Leaders

						            	(WPL)Microsoft Corporation", "subject": "Women Leaders’ Lunch on “Shaping Europe’s Competitiveness 
in the Digital Era”", "cabinet_member": "Sean MernaghPetra Nemeckova", "minutes_url": "https://ec.europa.eu/transparencyinitiative/meetings/exportmeetings.do?doc=df136492-d915-4cc1-92c7-0c14f95b7c03&host=no", "source_url": "https://ec.europa.eu/transparencyinitiative/meetings/meeting.do?host=5b0b3cd9-cf5f-48bf-b582-1d2dc6874a10&page=7", "actor_id": "COM_00006AC02D4F", "commissioner_name": "Teresa Ribera", "commissioner_portfolio": "clean, just and competitive transition in the second von der Leyen Commission", "host_id": "5b0b3cd9-cf5f-48bf-b582-1d2dc6874a10", "meeting_type": "cabinet", "id": "44d87644c9cf57c4", "minutes_subject": "matter: Women Leaders’ Lunch on “Shaping Europe’s Competitiveness in the Digital Era”", "points_raised": null, "conclusions": ": N/A", "ares_number": null, "transparency_register_ids": [], "commission_representatives": [{"name": "(s):", "function": null}, {"name": "Executive Vice-President Teresa Ribera", "function": null}, {"name": "Sean Mernagh", "function": "Member of Cabinet"}, {"name": "Petra Nemeckova", "function": "Member of Cabinet"}, {"name": "Name(s) of the", "function": null}, {"name": "interest", "function": null}, {"name": "representative(s):", "function": null}, {"name": "Women Political Leaders (WPL)", "function": null}, {"name": "Event co-hosted by Microsoft", "function": null}, {"name": "Subject matter: Women Leaders’ Lunch on “Shaping Europe’s Competitiveness", "function": null}, {"name": "in the Digital Era”", "function": null}, {"name": "Main points", "function": null}, {"name": "raised and", "function": null}, {"name": "positions", "function": null}, {"name": "expressed:", "function": null}, {"name": "• WPL offered some opening remarks and reflections on", "function": null}, {"name": "the topics of women in leadership and shaping Europe’s", "function": null}, {"name": "competitiveness in the digital era, including in relation", "function": null}, {"name": "to artificial intelligence (AI).", "function": null}, {"name": "• EVP Ribera was invited to share some perspectives on", "function": null}, {"name": "Europe’s competitiveness as being rooted in both the", "function": null}, {"name": "green and digital transitions, and the most important", "function": null}, {"name": "policy levers Europe must activate now to lead globally,", "function": null}, {"name": "such as in the areas of AI and clean technology.", "function": null}, {"name": "• EVP Ribera pointed out that that the green and digital", "function": null}, {"name": "transitions, in addition to being economic drivers, are", "function": null}, {"name": "essential for welfare and inclusive prosperity. As regards", "function": null}, {"name": "AI, since the technology and its uses are still evolving,", "function": null}, {"name": "we must remain vigilant to govern these technologies", "function": null}, {"name": "responsibly. As a final general remark EVP Ribera", "function": null}, {"name": "pointed that as the world experiences rapid changes, we", "function": null}, {"name": "must hold fast to the hard-won principles and values that", "function": null}, {"name": "form our foundation, and avoid being frozen by fear or", "function": null}, {"name": "drawn to oversimplified solutions.", "function": null}, {"name": "• In the ensuing roundtable discussion, each participant", "function": null}, {"name": "discussed certain elements they consider key for EU", "function": null}, {"name": "competitiveness.", "function": null}, {"name": "Conclusions: N/A", "function": null}]}

{"date_raw": "25/11/2025", "meeting_date": "2025-11-25", "location": "Brussels", "organizations": ["American Chamber of Commerce to the European Union"], "organizations_raw": "American Chamber of Commerce to the European Union

						            	(AmCham EU)", "subject": "Clean transition, Industrial Accelerator Act, Competition", "cabinet_member": "Miguel Gil Tertre, Thomas Woolfson", "minutes_url": "https://ec.europa.eu/transparencyinitiative/meetings/exportmeetings.do?doc=0e23df8d-5006-4ba4-ad7c-4cd4788af4e7&host=no", "source_url": "https://ec.europa.eu/transparencyinitiative/meetings/meeting.do?host=5b0b3cd9-cf5f-48bf-b582-1d2dc6874a10&page=4", "actor_id": "COM_00006AC02D4F", "commissioner_name": "Teresa Ribera", "commissioner_portfolio": "clean, just and competitive transition in the second von der Leyen Commission", "host_id": "5b0b3cd9-cf5f-48bf-b582-1d2dc6874a10", "meeting_type": "cabinet", "id": "48b8f3ef65ea4d15", "minutes_subject": "Clean transition, Industrial Accelerator Act, Competition", "points_raised": "- At a discussion organised by AmCham, the interest representatives shared their views on the EU’s climate and environmental transition and the role of the business community, on the upcoming Industrial Accelerator Act and European preference, and on competition policy including merger control and the Foreign Subsidies Regulation.
- The Commission representatives took note of the views shared and recalled Commission priorities for the mandate and for 2026, and informed on upcoming policy files.", "conclusions": null, "ares_number": null, "transparency_register_ids": [], "commission_representatives": [{"name": "(s):", "function": null}, {"name": "Miguel Gil Tertre", "function": "Head of Cabinet"}, {"name": "Thomas Woolfson", "function": "Member of Cabinet"}, {"name": "Name(s) of the", "function": null}, {"name": "(interest)", "function": null}, {"name": "representative(s):", "function": null}, {"name": "American Chamber of Commerce to the EU", "function": null}, {"name": "Subject matter: Clean transition, Industrial Accelerator Act, Competition", "function": null}, {"name": "Main points", "function": null}, {"name": "raised and", "function": null}, {"name": "positions", "function": null}, {"name": "expressed:", "function": null}, {"name": "• At a discussion organised by AmCham, the interest", "function": null}, {"name": "representatives shared their views on the EU’s climate and", "function": null}, {"name": "environmental transition and the role of the business community,", "function": null}, {"name": "on the upcoming Industrial Accelerator Act and European", "function": null}, {"name": "preference, and on competition policy including merger control", "function": null}, {"name": "and the Foreign Subsidies Regulation.", "function": null}, {"name": "• The Commission representatives took note of the views shared", "function": null}, {"name": "and recalled Commission priorities for the mandate and for", "function": null}, {"name": "2026, and informed on upcoming policy files.", "function": null}, {"name": "Conclusions: N/A", "function": null}]}

{"date_raw": "13/03/2025", "meeting_date": "2025-03-13", "location": "Brussels", "organizations_raw": "European Aluminium AISBL

						            	(European Aluminium)Befesa AluminioHammerer Aluminium Industries Holding GmbH

						            	(HAI)", "subject": "Exchange on challenges facing the aluminium industry in Europe", "cabinet_member": "Aleksandra Baranska", "minutes_url": "https://ec.europa.eu/transparencyinitiative/meetings/exportmeetings.do?doc=5989f498-b8d7-4564-9acf-a6e808653659&host=no", "source_url": "https://ec.europa.eu/transparencyinitiative/meetings/meeting.do?host=5b0b3cd9-cf5f-48bf-b582-1d2dc6874a10&page=16", "actor_id": "COM_00006AC02D4F", "commissioner_name": "Teresa Ribera", "commissioner_portfolio": "clean, just and competitive transition in the second von der Leyen Commission", "host_id": "5b0b3cd9-cf5f-48bf-b582-1d2dc6874a10", "meeting_type": "cabinet", "id": "4a1bad5b7efa09ef", "minutes_subject": "matter: Exchange on challenges facing the aluminium industry in Europe", "points_raised": null, "conclusions": ": N/A", "ares_number": null, "transparency_register_ids": [], "commission_representatives": [{"name": "(s):", "function": null}, {"name": "Executive Vice-President Teresa Ribera", "function": null}, {"name": "Aleksandra Barańska", "function": "Member of Cabinet"}, {"name": "Name(s) of the", "function": null}, {"name": "interest", "function": null}, {"name": "representative(s):", "function": null}, {"name": "European Aluminium AISBL", "function": null}, {"name": "Hammerer Aluminium Industries Holding GmbH", "function": null}, {"name": "Befesa Aluminio", "function": null}, {"name": "Subject matter: Exchange on challenges facing the aluminium industry in Europe", "function": null}, {"name": "Main points", "function": null}, {"name": "raised and", "function": null}, {"name": "positions", "function": null}, {"name": "expressed:", "function": null}, {"name": "• The interlocutors raised the immediate ‘existential crisis’ facing", "function": null}, {"name": "European aluminium recyclers, due to the leakage of scrap metal", "function": null}, {"name": "out of Europe. While demand for the product remains high,", "function": null}, {"name": "suppliers of scrap are selling to other markets like China, India", "function": null}, {"name": "and the US, which offer higher prices while protecting their own", "function": null}, {"name": "industry, e.g. via subsidies or tariffs.", "function": null}, {"name": "• This market distortion undermines the production of recycled", "function": null}, {"name": "aluminium in the EU and increases the risk that the EU ends up", "function": null}, {"name": "re-importing products made from EU scrap (e.g. solar panels,", "function": null}, {"name": "electric cars). The new US tariffs would likely exacerbate the", "function": null}, {"name": "situation, as countries like China or Turkey will pivot from the", "function": null}, {"name": "US market to seek their scrap metal from the EU market instead.", "function": null}, {"name": "•  The stakeholders called on urgent action by the Commission in", "function": null}, {"name": "a matter of months at the latest. The association would favour an", "function": null}, {"name": "export duty as a solution, allowing them to compete on a level", "function": null}, {"name": "playing field. They were confident that the WTO conditions were", "function": null}, {"name": "met. In contrast, the Foreign Subsidies Regulation was not seen", "function": null}, {"name": "as a useful tool to address the issue, nor were the existing trade", "function": null}, {"name": "defence measures deemed sufficient.", "function": null}, {"name": "• They also flagged the issue of heavily subsidised Chinese", "function": null}, {"name": "investment in EU neighbouring countries like Serbia, which was", "function": null}, {"name": "further undershooting EU prices and undermining the EU", "function": null}, {"name": "internal market.", "function": null}, {"name": "• The interlocutors stressed that contacts with the new", "function": null}, {"name": "Commission had been positive. The spirit of the Clean Industrial", "function": null}, {"name": "Deal was encouraging.", "function": null}, {"name": "• EVP Ribera expressed the Commission’s support for the", "function": null}, {"name": "concerns. She stressed that any trade measures would have to be", "function": null}, {"name": "WTO compatible. She also pointed to the potential of the", "function": null}, {"name": "Circular Economy Act in the medium term.", "function": null}, {"name": "Conclusions: N/A", "function": null}]}

